Step 1: Lock the IP in the Deco App
Open the Deco app on your phone.
Tap the More tab at the bottom right.
Tap Advanced.
Tap Address Reservation.
Tap the + (plus) icon in the top right corner.
Choose Select from Client.
Find the printer in the list. Based on your output, it's named BRW0022585BC472 with the MAC address 00-22-58-5B-C4-72. Check the box next to it.
Tap Done.
Optional: If you want to force it to stay 192.168.68.111, you can tap on the newly created reservation in the list, manually edit the IP address to .111, and tap Save.


*** Step 2: Stop Ubuntu from Auto-creating Broken Queues
Ubuntu has a background service that tries to "help" by auto-discovering printers, but for Brother printers, it usually configures them with the wrong protocol. Let's turn it off so you only use the stable connection you are about to build.
sudo systemctl stop cups-browsed
sudo systemctl disable cups-browsed


